From b1f7571932bbbd72ea4d0fb1d33f0b691011bf32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:39:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: wire up Brave Search key, stop Telegram Markdown
 crashes, parallelize search

- searchPositions() call site never passed env.BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY, so the
  bot always used the Bing RSS fallback even when a key was configured.
- TelegramClient now retries sendMessage/editMessageText as plain text when
  Telegram rejects unescaped Markdown in dynamic content (CV summaries,
  position titles, scraped snippets, names), instead of silently failing.
- searchPositions() now searches all sites in parallel instead of
  sequentially, cutting webhook response latency.
- Updated wrangler.toml and README.md, which still described the old
  DuckDuckGo scraping removed in an earlier commit.
- Added .gitignore (node_modules was untracked before, so this just makes it
  explicit for anyone running npm install locally).
